t(42, 1570, """Reading man .. the most dangerous knowledge a human can have .. that you live in your age and your time while reading humanity the right reading! Moving away from the right reading will distance any human from understanding reality and the future, and will make him take wrong decisions. One must strip oneself of the culture of rebelling against reality, so do not say Islam means living the life of the Companions. Can a Muslim of this age live the life of the Companions?! This is a dreamy romanticism, unrealistic, fit only for use in writing books! Do people realise that they basically understood the asceticism of the Companions wrongly?! And do they realise that not all the Companions were basically ascetics?! And do they realise that a period of time in which the Companions lived on little was so because basically their world was like that?! Basically their world was hard! Many Muslims do not realise that! And finally, do Muslims realise that the asceticism of the Companions did not basically make a huge difference between asceticism and the state of society?! Do many Muslims realise that the ascetic in the era of the Companions and the Followers was basically not separated from the state of society by a huge, great difference?! And do many Muslims realise that asceticism in the time of the Companions, in the form the Ummah grasped and learned and that reached it through what was transmitted of the reports of the first generation, do we realise that the asceticism of the Companions and the Followers was very possible in practice for men and women who were made by a real, hard making, which was never a making that resembles, not even by 0%, our own human making?!

When a Muslim talks to me with enthusiasm about the asceticism of the Companions, I smile! I smile and smile and smile, but suddenly I feel a problem! Not understanding reality is a problem, and not understanding the needs of the human of 2027 is a problem, and not grasping the psychological necessities of people in 2027, 90% of which were not psychological basics in the era of the Companions and the Followers, is a defect in human thinking today that must be treated, because this defect leads to a lack of clarity of vision regarding the nature of today's Muslim and today's human, and the psychological and physical needs newly arisen in today's world, which, had the Companions and the Followers known them, they would have mocked and said this is seeking the world, not seeking the Hereafter. For the Companions and the Followers were born in primitive eras and stone ages, and we were born in the time of radio and television. So asking the Muslim society to live a life of asceticism is an illogical request, and my asking even my own children to live asceticism is a request outside the grasp of the thinking of the human of 2027, who, even if his life stumbles at the level of technology and returns to the era of the seventies, this never means that he is ready to live the primitive stone age that helped the first Muslims turn more toward the Hereafter, although this turning, even if it happened in most of them, did not happen in all of them, for they too are humans. And a Companion or a Follower is never to be blamed if he took for himself a palace and a soft life from his pure lawful money; no one should forbid the blessing of Allah. But the Ummah, as it approaches 2027, should not exaggerate in theorising!""")

h(43, 350, """Islamic romanticism means believing that cloning the era of the Companions is possible! The human of this age is pampered and very weak!""")

t(43, 945, """What is wrong with a wedding in the morning, four hours before noon?! Will the tables, chairs and food in the morning, for example, object and say: No, we are used to weddings only at night, and we do not accept anyone using us in the morning?!

Or are wasting the prayers, staying up late, exhausting bodies and ruining the next day in production, worship and work among the hidden wisdoms that we do not know and that were hidden from us for centuries, for example, and that the common people knew, then spread, and they became the custom of all people, including the religious themselves?!""")

h(43, 1600, """The evening wedding party = the loss of the Maghrib and Isha prayers, the loss of the night prayer and the loss of the Fajr prayer for perhaps 99% of the guests!""")

t(43, 2125, """Doing this and that, doing what is done and what is not done, committing every calamity and disaster, oppressing people, eating the unlawful, and doing the deeds of devils of all kinds throughout the year, then listening to chants about love of the Prophet ﷺ, is hypocrisyyyyyyyyyyyy.""")

h(43, 2400, """The one who made a commotion against the Friday preacher of Aleppo: your commotion is respected on condition that the Prophet lives in you 365 days a year, so are you like that, to prove you are not a hypocrite?!""")

h(44, 950, """If you celebrate the Prophet's birthday while the Prophet is absent from most days of your year, the Prophet is innocent of your celebrating his birthday. Innocent of you, of your fake love and of this hypocrisy!""")

t(44, 1510, """Is it a celebration of the feeling of a guilty conscience? The guilt of conscience when any Muslim lives 364 days with his self, his whims and Satan, so he needs a day before the year ends to celebrate by remembering that there was a man named Muhammad ﷺ?!

Is it a celebration of patting the soul on the back after the self dragged it along and exhausted it for 364 days panting after the world?! What exactly is happening?!

Does the Prophet ﷺ not dwell in us? Is he not in us? Who said that I and those like me remember him only on the day of his birth?!

If others are like that, then I and others are innocent of it; we are not like that! We have nothing to do with that. By the grace of Allah the Exalted we do not need to remember him and celebrate his permanent presence in the world, alive when he was in it with his body, and alive when he died, so he remained alive in us. If we remember him every hour! We remember him every day! We remember him every evening! In every situation! Am I forced to remember him with those who forgot him for 364 days a year?!

What forces those who remember him 365 days a year to be equal with those who do not remember him for 364 days and remember him only one day a year?!

If they want that in their homes, they are free. But shame, shame .. a shame that this care for the Prophet does not happen for 365 days. If the Prophet ﷺ is not cared for in all 365 days of the year, then how bad are the successors after the predecessors.""")

h(45, 250, """I do not understand the Prophet's birthday, and my mind does not grasp it! My mind cannot take it in! I am a Muslim. I live with the Prophet 365 days a year, so when I am told to celebrate, I say: and what was I doing for 365 days?! I do not understand what they say! What do they mean by celebrating the Prophet's birthday?!""")

